<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Esen Taishi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1455">1455</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Esen Tayisi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Esen Taishi was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirat</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> who dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> in the mid-15th century, ruling through a puppet Genghisid khan. In 1449 he defeated a Ming army at Tumu and captured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhengtong-emperor">Zhengtong Emperor</a>. In 1453 he took the title of khan himself, breaking the rule that only descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> could be khan, but he was killed in 1455 and Oirat power declined.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/esen-taishi.jpg" alt="Esen Taishi" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Avishay · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ESENTAISH_KHAAN.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
